# Quick Start Guide
## Authentication Options
The chat app supports three authentication methods:
### 1. API Key (Easiest)
Get your API key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
**Option A** - Use .env file (recommended):
```bash
echo "GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_actual_key_here" > .env
```
**Option B** - Export as environment variable:
```bash
export GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_actual_key_here
```
**Option C** - Enter manually when prompted
### 2. OAuth (Gemini CLI)
- No setup required
- Browser will open automatically
- Sign in with your Google account
- Tokens saved to `.tokens.json`
- Same OAuth as official Gemini CLI
### 3. OAuth (Antigravity)
- No setup required
- Browser will open automatically
- Sign in with your Google account
- Tokens saved to `.tokens.json`
- Uses Google Cloud Code Assist credentials
## Run the Chat
```bash
bun start
```
## Example Session
```
🤖 Google Gemini Chat
? Choose authentication method: › 
  ❯ API Key (Simple & fast)
    OAuth (Gemini CLI) (Google OAuth for Gemini)
    OAuth (Antigravity) (Google Cloud Code Assist)
# If you choose API Key:
? Enter your Google API Key: › AIza...
# If you choose OAuth:
◇  Starting OAuth flow...
   [Browser opens automatically]
◆  ✓ OAuth authentication successful
? Select a model: › 
  ❯ Gemini 2.0 Flash (Experimental) (Latest & fastest)
    Gemini 1.5 Pro (Most capable)
    Gemini 1.5 Flash (Fast & efficient)
    Gemini 1.5 Flash 8B (Lightweight)
┌  Ready to chat
│  Model: Gemini 2.0 Flash (Experimental)
│  Type 'exit' or press Ctrl+C to quit
└
? You: › Hello! What can you help me with?
◇  Thinking...
◆  ✓ Response received
┌  🤖 Assistant
│  Hello! I'm a large language model, and I can help you with many things...
└
   Tokens: 12 in, 45 out
? You: › 
```
## Tips
- Press Ctrl+C or type `exit` to quit
- Chat history is maintained during the session
- Choose faster models (Flash, Flash 8B) for quicker responses
- Choose Pro models for more complex tasks
## Troubleshooting
### API Key Issues
**"Invalid API key format"**
- Make sure your key starts with "AIza"
- Check for extra spaces or quotes
**"API key not valid"**
- Verify the key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
- Make sure Gemini API is enabled for your project
### OAuth Issues
**"OAuth timeout"**
- Make sure you complete the browser sign-in within 5 minutes
- Check that ports 8085 (Gemini) or 51121 (Antigravity) are not in use
**"OAuth callback failed"**
- Ensure your browser can access localhost
- Try disabling VPN or firewall temporarily
- Check that the callback server can bind to the port
**"Token exchange failed"**
- Verify your Google account has appropriate permissions
- For Antigravity: Ensure Cloud Code Assist is enabled
### General Issues
**"Model not found"**
- Some models may not be available in all regions
- Try a different model from the list
**Port already in use**
- Close other applications using ports 8085 or 51121
- Or wait a moment and try again